What Swagger really is

• An auto-generated API interface
• Built from your FastAPI code
• Lets you:
  • See available endpoints
  • Understand request/response structure
  • Manually send requests

--------------------------------------------------

What Swagger is NOT

• Not your frontend
• Not used by real users
• Not part of production UI

--------------------------------------------------

What it replaces (temporarily)

Right now:
• Swagger = your “fake client”

In real apps:
• React / Web app / Mobile app = real client

--------------------------------------------------

Why Swagger exists

• To help developers:
  • Test endpoints quickly
  • Debug APIs
  • Understand data contracts

Without it, you'd need:
• Postman
• curl
• or custom frontend

--------------------------------------------------

Mental model

• Swagger = control panel for your API
• Not the product
• Just a developer tool

--------------------------------------------------

Real-world flow (no Swagger)

User → Frontend (UI)
      → sends HTTP request
      → FastAPI backend
      → returns JSON
      → Frontend updates UI

--------------------------------------------------

Key takeaway

• Swagger helps you build the backend
• It is NOT how your backend will be used in production
